  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP Thematic support to energy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The first phase of reconstruction efforts under the UNDP Resilience Building and Recovery Programme will focus on the restoration of essential utility services, including water and sanitation, solid waste management, and heating and energy supply. 

UNDP is working on 3 parallel streams on the Energy Crisis: 
&#x2022; Stream 1: Energy Sector Assessment:  supporting the Government of Ukraine and national partners for carrying out quantification of macro-economic impact of the Russian aggression. 
&#x2022; Stream 2: Provision of Emergency Equipment and support to urgent infrastructure repair for affected communities/regions: UNDP has been also providing emergency response through the immediate procurement and quick repair of generators, diesel oil, and other mobile energy items 
&#x2022; Stream 3: System procurement for mid- and long-term rehabilitation of the energy infrastructure.</narrative>
  </description>
